  </div>
  <div class="feature-item">
    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
      <line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"></line>
      <path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10z"></path>
    </svg>
    <span>IANA Africa/Johannesburg</span>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INTRODUCTION -->
<section class="acdt-intro content-section" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
  <h2 id="intro-heading" class="sr-only">About Greenwich Mean Time to South Africa Standard Time Conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Welcome to our comprehensive, standalone <strong>GMT to SAST Converter</strong>, designed specifically for software engineers, financial traders, travel planners, and international business managers operating across Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) and South Africa Standard Time (UTC+2). South Africa Standard Time is observed continuously throughout South Africa, Eswatini, and Lesotho without daylight saving time shifts, establishing a fixed, predictable 2-hour offset ahead of GMT.
  </p>
  <p>
    Greenwich Mean Time serves as the fundamental astronomical reference point calculated at the Royal Observatory in Greenwich, London. Because GMT remains unadjusted for seasonal clock changes, it serves as the ultimate baseline for international database architectures, cloud server telemetry, aviation flight logging, and cross-border maritime shipping across Atlantic and Indian Ocean trade routes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Coordinating schedules between GMT and SAST is exceptionally smooth because both regions share virtually the same longitudinal meridian. Whether you are executing financial trades on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange (JSE), arranging wildlife safari itineraries in Kruger National Park, or coordinating technical sprint demos between London and Cape Town, this guide and interactive calculator ensure complete precision.
  </p>
  <p>
    In this detailed resource, you will find interactive live clocks, a customizable conversion calculator, an hourly 24-hour reference table, cross-border meeting planner recommendations, and in-depth explanations of regional timekeeping standards.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- INTERACTIVE CONVERTER & HERO GRAPHIC -->
<section class="hero" id="converter-section" aria-labelledby="converter-tool-heading">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Conversion Tool</p>
    <h2 id="converter-tool-heading">Convert GMT to South Africa Standard Time</h2>
    <p>
      Select any time in GMT to instantly calculate the corresponding South Africa Standard Time. Our converter utilizes browser-native timezone logic for precise calculations across all calendar dates.
    </p>

    <div class="custom-svg-container" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 600 240" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
        <rect width="600" height="240" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
        <path d="M0 40 H600 M0 80 H600 M0 120 H600 M0 160 H600 M0 200 H600" stroke="#12455d" stroke-width="1" />
        
        <!-- GMT Node -->
        <g transform="translate(150, 120)">
          <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#2f6278" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="0" y="-10" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="18" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT</text>
          <text x="0" y="15" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">UTC+0</text>
          <text x="0" y="32" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">Greenwich Meridian</text>
        </g>
        <!-- Arrow + Offset -->
        <g transform="translate(300, 120)">
          <line x1="-50" y1="0" x2="50" y2="0" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="6,4"/>
          <polygon points="45,-6 55,0 45,6" fill="#36c7b5"/>
          <rect x="-45" y="-22" width="90" height="24" fill="#1b536e" rx="4"/>
          <text x="0" y="-6" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">+2 Hours Ahead</text>
        </g>
        <!-- SAST Node -->
        <g transform="translate(450, 120)">
          <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="55" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="0" y="-10" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="18" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">SAST</text>
          <text x="0" y="15" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">UTC+2</text>
          <text x="0" y="32" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#bdd2dc" text-anchor="middle">South Africa</text>
