</section>

<!-- TIME DIFFERENCE & CALCULATION METHODS -->
<section class="method-section content-section" id="calculation-methods" aria-labelledby="methods-heading">
  <h2 id="methods-heading">How to Calculate GMT to SAST Time Differences</h2>
  <p class="method-intro">
    Calculating the time in South Africa from GMT is exceptionally straightforward: add exactly 2 hours to the Greenwich time. Because neither GMT nor SAST observes seasonal daylight saving clock shifts in their standard baseline definitions, this 2-hour offset remains constant 365 days a year.
  </p>

  <div class="custom-svg-container" style="margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 200" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="200" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <text x="350" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="15" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">GMT to SAST 24-Hour Timeline Comparison</text>
      <!-- GMT Bar -->
      <rect x="50" y="65" width="600" height="34" fill="#12455d" rx="4"/>
      <text x="70" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">GMT: 08:00 AM</text>
      <text x="350" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">12:00 PM (Noon)</text>
      <text x="600" y="87" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#f4fbff">05:00 PM</text>
      <!-- SAST Bar -->
      <rect x="50" y="125" width="600" height="34" fill="#1b536e" rx="4"/>
      <text x="70" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">SAST: 10:00 AM</text>
      <text x="350" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">02:00 PM</text>
      <text x="600" y="147" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5">07:00 PM</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Simple +2 Addition Formula</h3>
      <p>Take any GMT hour value and add 2 hours. For example, 09:00 AM GMT + 2 hours = 11:00 AM SAST. If the total exceeds 24:00, subtract 24 to determine the time on the subsequent morning.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Shared Meridian Advantage</h3>
      <p>Greenwich (0° longitude) and South Africa (approx 28° E longitude) share almost the same longitude meridian. This close alignment minimizes solar variance and makes scheduling intuitive.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. Zero Daylight Saving Shifts</h3>
      <p>South Africa maintains UTC+2 year-round without daylight saving adjustments. This eliminates the confusion caused by seasonal clock changes in other international regions.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>4. British Summer Time (BST) Distinction</h3>
      <p>Be aware that when London observes British Summer Time (BST, UTC+1) between March and October, London local time is 1 hour behind SAST, whereas standard GMT remains 2 hours behind SAST.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STEP BY STEP GUIDE -->
<section class="content-section" id="step-by-step-guide" aria-labelledby="step-heading">
  <h2 id="step-heading">Step-by-Step Guide for Converting GMT to SAST</h2>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 1: Obtain the Source GMT Timestamp</h3>
      <p>Identify your starting Greenwich Mean Time. GMT is calculated relative to 0° longitude and does not change with the seasons.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 2: Add 2 Hours for South Africa Standard Time</h3>
      <p>Perform the simple mathematical addition of 2 hours. For example, 14:00 GMT becomes 16:00 SAST.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 3: Confirm Date Boundary Shifts</h3>
      <p>If your GMT time is 22:00 or 23:00, adding 2 hours shifts the SAST time to 00:00 or 01:00 of the following day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Step 4: Verify Target Region Offset</h3>
      <p>Ensure your target city is in South Africa, Eswatini, or Lesotho to confirm adherence to the UTC+2 SAST rule.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

