<!-- MEETING PLANNER -->
<section class="method-section content-section" id="meeting-planner" aria-labelledby="planner-heading">
  <h2 id="planner-heading">GMT to SAST Meeting Planner & Overlap Strategy</h2>
  <p class="method-intro">
    Because South Africa is only 2 hours ahead of Greenwich Mean Time, scheduling meetings between London, Western Europe, and South Africa is exceptionally convenient. Below are recommended meeting slots tailored for business efficiency.
  </p>

  <div class="custom-svg-container" style="margin: 1.5rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 160" width="100%" height="auto" style="display: block;">
      <rect width="700" height="160" fill="#0c354a" rx="8" />
      <!-- Golden Window Highlight -->
      <rect x="180" y="40" width="340" height="80" fill="rgba(54, 199, 181, 0.12)" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4" rx="6"/>
      <text x="350" y="30" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="13" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">Optimal Crossover Window: 08:00 - 15:00 GMT (10:00 - 17:00 SAST)</text>
      
      <g transform="translate(100, 80)">
        <text x="0" y="0" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">GMT Morning</text>
        <text x="0" y="20" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">08:00 AM GMT</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(350, 80)">
        <text x="0" y="0" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">Midday Synchronization</text>
        <text x="0" y="20" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">12:00 PM GMT = 02:00 PM SAST</text>
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(600, 80)">
        <text x="0" y="0" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="14" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">SAST Close</text>
        <text x="0" y="20" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#8fd7ff" text-anchor="middle">05:00 PM SAST</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>1. Morning Standup Window</h3>
      <p>Schedule morning alignment calls at 08:30 AM GMT (10:30 AM SAST). South African team members have already cleared morning emails, while UK/GMT participants are starting their workday.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>2. Midday Strategy & Workshop Slot</h3>
      <p>11:00 AM GMT corresponds to 01:00 PM SAST. This slot allows for deep-dive technical reviews, vendor presentations, and executive board meetings without disrupting lunch routines.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>3. End-of-Day Handover Slot</h3>
      <p>03:00 PM GMT matches 05:00 PM SAST. South African employees can deliver daily code commits or project updates right before wrapping up their business day.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>4. Zero Fatigue Executive Travel</h3>
      <p>Business leaders traveling between London and Johannesburg experience zero fatigue from timezone displacement, ensuring immediate productivity upon arrival.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INDUSTRY & REGIONAL USE CASES -->
<section class="content" id="use-cases" aria-labelledby="usecases-heading">
  <h2 id="usecases-heading">Industry Applications & Cross-Border Scenarios</h2>
  <article>
    <h3>Johannesburg Stock Exchange (JSE) & European Capital Markets</h3>
    <p>
      The Johannesburg Stock Exchange operates standard trading sessions between 09:00 AM and 05:00 PM SAST (07:00 AM to 03:00 PM GMT). This offers near-perfect overlap with major European financial centers, facilitating liquidity streaming, cross-border equity trading, and simultaneous economic announcement releases.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>Offshore Software Development & Business Process Outsourcing (BPO)</h3>
    <p>
      South Africa—particularly Cape Town, Johannesburg, and Durban—has developed into a global hub for UK and European software engineering and customer experience centers. Native English fluency combined with a minor 2-hour offset enables real-time pair programming, continuous integration monitoring, and direct customer support.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>International Tourism, Safaris & Flight Logistics</h3>
    <p>
      Over 1 million European travelers visit Southern Africa annually for wildlife safaris and coastal tourism. Direct long-haul flights from London Heathrow (LHR) to O.R. Tambo International Airport (JNB) or Cape Town International Airport (CPT) run north-to-south, allowing passengers to sleep overnight and arrive with zero jet lag.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>Mining, Energy Sector & Supply Chain Management</h3>
    <p>
      South Africa is a world-leading producer of platinum, gold, and manganese. Global mining conglomerates headquartered in London coordinate daily extraction targets, safety audits, and shipping logistics directly with mine operators in Rustenburg and Witbank using real-time GMT-to-SAST communications.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>Academic Research & Agricultural Telemetry</h3>
